## Edict Workflow

Tools teach their own commands:{% if tools.bones %} bones `bn tldr` ·{% endif %}{% if tools.maw %} maw `maw tldr` (`maw --help`) ·{% endif %}{% if tools.seal %} seal `seal --help` ·{% endif %}{% if tools.rite %} rite `rite tldr` ·{% endif %} edict `edict protocol --help`. Some tool docs are out of date: where a tool's quick start differs from the Rules below, the Rules win. Identity: `$AGENT`, set by the launcher; manual sessions use `<project>-dev`.
{% if tools.maw %}
Layout: {% if is_root_layout %}the repo root is the trunk (the `default` workspace); agent workspaces live in `.maw/workspaces/<name>/`.{% else %}bare repo: the trunk is `ws/default/`; agent workspaces live in `ws/<name>/`.{% endif %}
{% endif %}
### Rules
{% if tools.bones %}
- **Track all work in a bone.** Create it before you start (`{{ bn }} create`), move it `open` → `doing` → `done`, and post progress comments for crash recovery. See [update.md](.agents/edict/update.md).
{%- endif %}
{%- if tools.maw %}
- **Edit only in a maw workspace** named after the {% if tools.bones %}bone{% else %}task{% endif %}: `maw ws create {{ ws }} --from main`, then work in `{{ ws_prefix }}{{ ws }}/`. Never edit {% if is_root_layout %}the trunk at the repo root{% else %}`ws/default/`{% endif %} directly, and never create git branches: maw workspaces replace them. See [start.md](.agents/edict/start.md).
- **Run each tool in its place.** Run commands in a workspace with `maw exec <ws> -- <cmd>`.{% if tools.bones %} {% if is_root_layout %}Run `bn` directly at the repo root.{% else %}Run bones through `maw exec default -- bn`.{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if tools.seal %} Run seal through `maw exec <ws> -- seal`.{% endif %}
- **Never merge or destroy `default`.** It is the merge target.
{%- endif %}
- **Run the edict protocol at each transition:** `edict protocol resume|start|review|finish|merge|cleanup … --agent $AGENT`, then run the steps it prints, in order. If it exits 1, follow the matching workflow doc below.
{%- if tools.maw %}
- **Reviewed work merges only through `edict protocol merge <ws> --message "feat: …"`.** A bare `maw ws merge` skips the review log, the clean check and the `risk:critical` gate; use it only for work with no review.{% if seal_review %} Commit no code after the LGTM, only the review log.{% endif %} See [merge-check.md](.agents/edict/merge-check.md#the-review-log-and-the-clean-check).
- **A conflicted workspace is a normal state, not a failure:** `maw ws resolve <ws> --list`. See [merge-check.md](.agents/edict/merge-check.md#conflict-recovery).
- **Run `maw ws recover` before you conclude work is lost** or start a {% if tools.bones %}bone{% else %}task{% endif %} over. Destroyed workspaces keep snapshots. See [worker-loop.md](.agents/edict/worker-loop.md).
{%- endif %}
{%- if seal_review %}
- **Seal completion is not approval.** Confirm the verdict with `seal review <id> --format json`. `--reviewers` spawns nobody; for security review follow [security-review.md](.agents/edict/security-review.md#who-sends-what), and never mention `@<project>-security`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if tools.rite %}
- **Answer `$RITE_MESSAGE_ID` with `--reply-to`.** Never reuse the anchor from an earlier turn. See [cross-channel.md](.agents/edict/cross-channel.md#threads).
- **Ask, then wait on the anchor:** capture the id you sent (`--format json`), then `rite wait --reply-to <id> -t 300`. On exit 1, post one `-L task-blocked` and move on; never re-send. Stuck on a companion tool? Ask its project channel this way. See [cross-channel.md](.agents/edict/cross-channel.md#ask-and-wait).
- **Rite messages are one labelled line that leads with the bone id**, e.g. `-L task-blocked "<bone-id>: blocked on <thing>, needs <what unblocks it>"`. No status blocks or recaps. See [cross-channel.md](.agents/edict/cross-channel.md#message-shape).
{%- endif %}
- **Run {% if check_command %}`{{ check_command }}`{% else %}the project's check command{% endif %} before committing**, and fix failures first. Workers do not push; the lead merges and pushes. See [finish.md](.agents/edict/finish.md).
- **Confirm before destructive actions** (deleting data, force-pushing, discarding unmerged work): ask the human first.
